   Cell penetrating peptides (CPP) that are featured by their ability to
   penetrate the membrane of different microorganisms. They were identified
   using the polarity index method described in Sect. 3.3. For this purpose
   two classifications were taken into account: non endocytic and endocytic
   pathway uptake mechanisms. The peptides studied were taken from CPPsite
   Database (CPPsite), and the set of selective cationic amphipatic
   antibacterial peptides (SCAAP) described in Sect. 6.3.3. The comparative
   study of these two groups made possible the identification of a
   particular reason for the toxicity of the selective cationic amphipatic
   antibacterial peptides.},
