   nov., are described and illustrated. The new genus possesses all
   characters of the tribe Sensillanurini Cassagnau, and is characterised
   by the presence of slightly elongated tubercles on the body and also
   elongation and thickening of the sensillum S2 as well as S7 on antennal
   segment IV. Development of S7 is a character of the tribe.},
