Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {Let M-n be a compact oriented hypersurface of a unit sphere Sn+1(1) with
   constant mean curvature H. Given an integer k between 2 and n - 1, we
   introduce a tensor f related to H and to the second fundamental form A
   of M, and show that if vertical bar phi vertical bar(2) <= B-H,B-k and
   tr(phi(3)) <= C-n,C-k vertical bar phi vertical bar(3), where B-H,B-k
   and C-n,C-k are numbers depending only on H, n and k, then either
   vertical bar phi vertical bar(2)  0 or vertical bar phi vertical bar(2) 
   B-H,B-k. We characterize all M-n with vertical bar phi vertical bar(2) 
   B-H,B-k. We also prove that if vertical bar A vertical bar(2) <= 2 root
   k(n - k) and tr(phi(3)) <= C-n,C-k vertical bar f vertical bar(3) then
   vertical bar A vertical bar(2) is constant and characterize all M-n with
   vertical bar A vertical bar(2) in the interval {[}0, 2 root k( n - k)].
   We also study the behavior of vertical bar phi vertical bar(2), with the
   condition additional tr(phi(3)) <= C-n,k vertical bar phi vertical
   bar(3), for complete hypersurfaces with constant mean curvature immersed
   in space forms and show that if sup(M) vertical bar phi vertical bar(2)
   = BH, k and this supremum is attained in M-n then M-n is an
   isoparametric hypersurface with two distinct principal curvatures of
   multiplicities k y n - k.
   Finally, we use rotation hypersurfaces to show that the condition on the
   trace of phi(3) is necessary in our results; more precisely, for each
   integer k with 2 <= k <= n - 1 and H >= 1/root 2n - 1 there is a
   complete hypersurface M-n in Sn+1(1) with constant mean curvature H such
   that sup(M) vertical bar phi vertical bar(2) = B-H,B-k, and this
   supremum is attained in M-n, and which is not a product of spheres.},
